jobs.description:
Are you looking for a varied role in the manufacturing industry? Then we’re looking for you to work for a client in Ittervoort. This is a position as an operator on the mixing line, working in a 3-shift rotation. This means you’ll be responsible for assembling orders. You’ll ensure that the logistics process runs smoothly and that everything is put together properly. Your daily responsibilities will include the following:

- You’ll create the correct combinations and place the products together in the packaging;
- You’ll check that the packages are complete and undamaged as they’re loaded onto the pallets;
- Occasionally moving products with a forklift.

This is a three-shift position, Monday through Friday. You will work the following shifts: 5:54 a.m.–2:00 p.m., 1:54 p.m.–10:00 p.m., 9:54 p.m.–6:00 a.m. (7.36 paid hours).

- You are fluent in Dutch or English;
- You have experience with production work;
- You have experience operating a forklift.
- Would you like to further your career in production? Then we’re looking for you!

We are looking for a Logistics Reception & Expedition Employee for our logistics department. In this versatile role, you will be the first point of contact for drivers and ensure that incoming and outgoing goods flow smoothly and correctly.

- Receiving and registering drivers and visitors;
- Coordinating incoming and outgoing goods;
- Checking freight documents and transport documentation;
- Administrative processing in the logistics system;
- Managing loading and unloading processes;
- Assisting with loading and unloading;
- Ensuring order, cleanliness, and safety in the dispatch area.

- Experience in a logistics role;
- Experience with an EPT, forklift, or reach truck;
- Good communication skills;
- Accurate and stress-resistant work ethic;
- Basic knowledge of MS Office and logistics systems;
- You speak the English language.

For our client in Kessel, we are looking for a production employee for the Maintenance and Laundry department. In this role, you’ll be responsible for inspecting used materials for quality, cleaning them, packaging, and getting them ready for transport or storage. You'll work with modern machinery to ensure the customer receives rental items that are complete, clean, and undamaged. You’ll be handling various tent components such as floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases, cleaning them both manually and with machines. Familiarity with industrial machinery and using a high-pressure cleaner is essential.

Your tasks will include:

- Washing and maintaining tent components and rental materials (e.g., floors, walls, doors, windows, and canvases) by machine and hand;
- Operating industrial washers, dryers, high-pressure cleaners, and overhead cranes;
- Monitoring product quality and detecting any damages;
- Inspecting and packing canvases;
- Preparing materials for storage or transport;
- Maintaining a safe and sustainable workspace.

You will be working in an international environment where Dutch and English are the primary languages. Working hours are from 07:00 to 15:30, Monday through Friday.

We are seeking someone with experience in an industrial production setting and a hands-on approach. You’re not afraid to roll up your sleeves and tackle physical tasks. Additionally, you possess:

- A completed VMBO or basic vocational education (level 2) or an equivalent qualification;
- Good command of Dutch or English;
- A forklift certification, or you’re willing to obtain one;
- A desire to grow by participating in internal training opportunities.
